From a3c9210e014ff8902f61518a9a811121859ff2f2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: shorinkiwata <fcl709@outlook.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 20:07:17 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] d3dcompiler: Handle the ISG1, OSG1 and PSG1 signature chunks.

Shaders that use min16float, min16int or min16uint anywhere in a
signature are written with ISG1/OSG1/PSG1 instead of ISGN/OSGN/PCSG.
Each element has two more fields than an ISGN element: the stream index
before the semantic name offset, and the minimum precision after the
mask.

Reflection skipped these chunks, so such a shader reported no input or
output parameters, and D3DGetBlobPart() failed to extract its
signatures. An application that builds its input layout from the
reflected input signature ended up with an empty layout, which pipeline
creation rightly rejects.

Parse the chunks with the 8-field layout and report MinPrecision from
them; ISGN, OSGN and PCSG keep D3D_MIN_PRECISION_DEFAULT. Element sizes
other than 6 now always skip the stream field, also in the D3D10 build
where the structure has no Stream member.

The tests use shaders compiled with d3dcompiler_47 and pass on Windows.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
